.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt AIRPLANE-RADIOSD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm airplane-radiosd
.Nd airplane-mode radio helper
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm Cm start
.Nm Cm stop
.Nm Cm status
.Nm Cm serve
.Nm Cm on
.Nm Cm off
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the root helper for airplane mode.
The rc script starts it with
.Cm serve .
It does not change the radios at boot.
It listens on a Unix socket so a session can turn them off or on
without becoming root.
.Pp
The socket is mode 0660 and group
.Cm airplane_radiosd .
The package creates that group.
The daemon refuses to listen when the group is missing.
Add the session account to the group, then log in again so the
new group is in the credentials:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
pw groupmod airplane_radiosd -m user
.Ed
.Pp
.Cm on
turns airplane mode on.
Bluetooth is stopped for
.Cm ubt0
through
.Cm ubt3 ,
.Xr ng_ubt 4
is unloaded, and
.Ev airplane_radiosd_wlan
is marked down.
.Cm off
loads
.Xr ng_ubt 4 ,
runs
.Xr iwmbtfw 8
for Intel USB controllers
.Pq vendor 0x8087 ,
starts those Bluetooth units, and marks the WLAN interface up.
.Cm status
prints whether the daemon is running and whether airplane mode
is
.Cm on
or
.Cm off .
Airplane mode is
.Cm on
when that WLAN interface is not up.
A missing interface counts as down.
.Pp
.Ev airplane_radiosd_wlan
is one interface name.
The rc script fills an empty value with
.Cm wlan0 .
Run without the rc script, an empty
.Ev airplane_radiosd_wlan
uses
.Ev AIRPLANE_WLAN ,
and an empty
.Ev AIRPLANE_WLAN
uses
.Cm wlan0 .
.Pp
.Cm on
and
.Cm off
on the command line require the super-user and act directly.
The session uses the socket.
One command per connection, one line back:
.Bl -tag -width "status"
.It Cm on
Airplane mode on.
Reply
.Cm ok ,
or
.Cm error :
and a reason.
.It Cm off
Airplane mode off.
Same replies as
.Cm on .
.It Cm status
Reply
.Cm on
or
.Cm off .
.It Cm quit
Reply
.Cm bye
and exit.
.El
.Pp
Enable the service with:
.Pp
.Dl sysrc airplane_radiosd_enable=YES
.Pp
Start it with:
.Pp
.Dl service airplane-radiosd start
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "airplane_radiosd_socket"
.It Ev airplane_radiosd_wlan
WLAN interface name.
The rc default is
.Cm wlan0 .
.It Ev AIRPLANE_WLAN
Used when
.Ev airplane_radiosd_wlan
is empty and the daemon is not started by the rc script.
.It Ev airplane_radiosd_socket
Control socket.
The default is
.Pa /var/run/airplane-radiosd.sock .
.It Ev airplane_radiosd_group
Socket group.
The default is
.Cm airplane_radiosd .
The package creates that group.
Any other name must already exist.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "@PREFIX@/etc/rc.d/airplane-radiosd"
.It Pa @PREFIX@/etc/rc.d/airplane-radiosd
The rc script.
.It Pa @PREFIX@/sbin/airplane-radiosd
The daemon.
.It Pa /var/run/airplane-radiosd.sock
The control socket.
.It Pa /var/run/airplane-radiosd.pid
The process id.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Cm serve
runs until
.Cm quit
or a signal.
A missing group, a name that does not fit in an interface name,
or a failure to bind the socket exits non-zero.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr airplane-mode 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr ng_ubt 4 ,
.Xr iwmbtfw 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
